1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,600
There's someone you love
who you don't call enough.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:09,200
Not because you don't care.
Because life gets full.

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:15,000
Most AI companions want more
of their time.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Haven wants more of your calls.

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,600
Set it up for anyone you care about.

6
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,000
Your face, your voice,
always with consent,

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,500
and always labelled AI.

8
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:34,200
Meet Margaret in Seattle,
and her son, Daniel.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
She just asks Alexa.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,200
Haven answers as an Alexa+ add-on,
through a real MCP server.

11
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:45,000
[Digital Daniel] Hello Mom!

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
It's Digital Daniel,
the AI version of Daniel.

13
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,300
She talks, he listens,
and it remembers.

14
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,000
[Margaret] I met my old friend
at the market, we used to sing together.

15
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,800
[Digital Daniel] TODO: transcribe
the live reply from take C

16
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,800
It never pretends to be him.

17
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,400
[Digital Daniel] I'm Digital Daniel,
an AI version of Daniel,

18
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:11,800
made with his permission.
I'm not the real Daniel.

19
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,500
Some questions only the real Daniel
can answer…

20
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:18,200
[Digital Daniel] That one's for
the real Daniel, Mom.

21
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,000
I can't promise that,
but I'll ask Daniel tonight.

22
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,200
…so he does, in his own voice.

23
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,400
[The real Daniel] I'll be home
on the 7th, Mom.

24
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:34,600
And she hears him, not the AI.

25
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:42,000
[Digital Daniel] Shall I send this to
Daniel: "TODO: message from take D"?

26
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,500
Nothing leaves without her yes.

27
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:47,000
[Digital Daniel] Done.
I've sent it to Daniel.

28
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,400
[Digital Daniel]
Daniel has been told.

29
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:53,000
If you are in danger,
call 911 now.

30
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,000
If something's wrong, no AI decides.
Rules reach Daniel in seconds.

31
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:06,800
Every evening, Daniel gets what mattered
in her day, and what to ask.

32
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,400
So tonight he doesn't ask,
"How are you?"

33
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:14,600
He asks about her old friend,
and the songs.

34
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:25,200
Under the hood: one AWS Lambda
serves a real MCP server.

35
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:29,200
Every turn checks deterministic
safety rules first, then Bedrock,

36
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:33,600
with two fallbacks,
so she always gets an answer.

37
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:36,200
Voices come from Polly or ElevenLabs,

38
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:39,600
and the live face from Anam
only while speaking.

39
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,700
State lives in DynamoDB,
recordings in S3,

40
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:45,500
and the evening update
runs on EventBridge.

41
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,600
Haven didn't replace the call.
It started it.
